/-!
# Flatness and tensor products

Mathlib's `TensorProduct.map_injective_of_flat_flat` shows that the tensor product of two
injective linear maps is injective when the codomain of the first and the domain of the second
are flat. This file records the same statement for `Algebra.TensorProduct.map` of algebra
homomorphisms, so that it applies without first passing to the underlying linear maps.
It also identifies the kernel after tensoring an algebra map with a flat algebra, the analogue
of Mathlib's `Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor_ker` with flatness in place of surjectivity.
For two algebra maps, flatness of the first codomain and the second kernel quotient similarly
identifies the tensor-product kernel with the ideal generated by the two kernels.

Finally, if `R → B` is a map of commutative semirings, `A` is a flat `B`-module, and `M` is a
`B`-module that is flat over `R`, then `A ⊗[B] M` is flat over `R`. A localization `B_q ⊗[B] M`
of an `R`-flat module over a ring is the typical case. Over semirings, flatness here means
mono-flatness, as in Mathlib's `Module.Flat`. In particular, for an ideal `J` of `B` with
`B ⧸ J` flat over `R`, `C ⧸ J C` is flat over `R` for every flat `B`-algebra `C`.

For an injective `f : N →ₗ[R] P`, an element of `M ⊗[R] N` killed by `f.lTensor M` is also killed
by `ψ.rTensor N` for any map `ψ` from `M` to a flat module.

Two injectivity statements for tensoring with a module `M` over a ring are the diagram-chasing
steps of the local criterion for flatness. If `f.rTensor M` is injective and `F` is flat, then so
is `(f.rTensor F).rTensor M`. If `M ⧸ I M` is flat over `R ⧸ I`, then tensoring with `M` preserves
injectivity of maps between modules killed by `I`. If moreover `I ⊗[R] M → M` is injective, that
is `Tor₁ᴿ(R ⧸ I, M) = 0`, then `N ⊗[R] M → L ⊗[R] M` is injective whenever `L ⧸ N` is killed by a
power of `I`. Cover `L` by a free module `F` and let `G` be the preimage of `N`; for `G ⊇ I F`,
`I F ⊗ M → F ⊗ M` is injective because `F` is flat, and two diagram chases replace the long exact
`Tor` sequences of the textbook argument. Applied to `J ⧸ (J ⊓ Iⁿ)` inside `R ⧸ Iⁿ`, this shows
that the kernel of `J ⊗[R] M → M` comes from `(J ⊓ Iⁿ) ⊗[R] M`, the step of the local criterion
for flatness before the Artin–Rees lemma. For any ideal `P` in place of `Iⁿ`, the same conclusion
holds without the `Tor₁` hypothesis when `M ⧸ P M` is flat over `R ⧸ P`, since `J ⧸ (J ⊓ P)` and
`R ⧸ P` are both killed by `P`.

If `M` is flat at every prime outside the zero locus of a scalar `a`, powers of `a` kill
each tensor kernel induced by an injective map. The quotient-ring variant applies to maps
between modules annihilated by the quotient ideal, as in generic-freeness arguments.

## Main results

* `Module.pow_smul_eq_zero_of_flat_localizedModule`: local flatness away from `a` makes tensor
  kernels `a`-power torsion. The quotient variant applies to annihilated modules.

* `Algebra.TensorProduct.map_injective_of_flat_flat`: the tensor product of two injective algebra
  homomorphisms is injective under the flatness hypotheses of
  `TensorProduct.map_injective_of_flat_flat`.
* `Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor_ker_of_flat`: tensoring with a flat algebra carries kernels
  to their images under the right tensor inclusion.
* `Algebra.TensorProduct.map_ker_of_flat_flat`: the kernel of a tensor product of algebra maps
  is generated by their kernels when the first codomain and the second kernel quotient are flat.
* `Module.Flat.tensorProduct_of_flat`: if `A` is flat over `B` and `M` is flat over `R`, then
  `A ⊗[B] M` is flat over `R`.
* `Module.Flat.quotient_map_algebraMap`: if `C` is a flat `B`-algebra and `B ⧸ J` is flat over
  `R`, then `C ⧸ J C` is flat over `R`.
* `Module.Flat.rTensor_rTensor_injective`: tensoring with a flat module preserves injectivity of
  `f.rTensor M`, over any commutative semiring.
* `Module.Flat.rTensor_apply_eq_zero_of_lTensor_apply_eq_zero`: an element of `M ⊗[R] N` killed
  by `f.lTensor M` for an injective `f` is killed by `ψ.rTensor N` for every map `ψ` from `M` to a
  flat module.
* `Ideal.rTensor_injective_of_isTorsionBySet`: if `M ⧸ I M` is flat over `R ⧸ I`, tensoring
  with `M` preserves injectivity of maps into a module killed by `I`.
* `Ideal.subtype_rTensor_injective_of_pow_smul_top_le`: if moreover `Tor₁ᴿ(R ⧸ I, M) = 0`, then
  `N ⊗[R] M → L ⊗[R] M` is injective whenever `I ^ n` kills `L ⧸ N`;
  `Ideal.subtype_rTensor_injective_of_smul_top_le` is the case `n = 1`.
* `Ideal.mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_pow`: under the same hypotheses, the kernel of
  `J ⊗[R] M → M` comes from `(J ⊓ I ^ n) ⊗[R] M`.
* `Ideal.mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_of_flat`: for an ideal `P` with `M ⧸ P M` flat over
  `R ⧸ P`, the kernel of `J ⊗[R] M → M` comes from `(J ⊓ P) ⊗[R] M`.
* `RingHom.injective_comp_include_of_disjoint_nonZeroDivisors`: a ring map out of a tensor product
  of flat domains whose kernel contains no nonzerodivisor is injective on both factors.
-/

public section

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Algebra.TensorProduct

section Semiring

variable {R S A B C D : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommSemiring S] [Algebra R S]
variable [Semiring A] [Semiring B] [Semiring C] [Semiring D]
variable [Algebra R A] [Algebra R B] [Algebra R C] [Algebra R D]
variable [Algebra S A] [Algebra S B] [IsScalarTower R S A] [IsScalarTower R S B]

/-- The tensor product of two injective algebra homomorphisms is injective when the codomain of
the first and the domain of the second are flat. -/
theorem map_injective_of_flat_flat (f : A →ₐ[S] B) (g : C →ₐ[R] D)
    [Module.Flat R B] [Module.Flat R C]
    (hf : Function.Injective f) (hg : Function.Injective g) :
    Function.Injective (map f g) :=
  -- `map f g` is `TensorProduct.map` of the underlying `R`-linear maps by definition.
  _root_.TensorProduct.map_injective_of_flat_flat (f.toLinearMap.restrictScalars R)
    g.toLinearMap hf hg

end Semiring

section Ring

variable {R A B C : Type*} [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Ring B] [Ring C]
variable [Algebra R A] [Algebra R B] [Algebra R C]

/-- Tensoring an algebra map with a flat algebra carries its kernel to the ideal generated
by its image under the right tensor inclusion. -/
theorem lTensor_ker_of_flat [Module.Flat R A] (f : B →ₐ[R] C) :
    RingHom.ker (map (AlgHom.id R A) f) =
      (RingHom.ker f).map (includeRight : B →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] B) := by
  rw [← Submodule.restrictScalars_inj R, Ideal.map_includeRight_eq]
  -- Restricted to `R`, `RingHom.ker` of `map (AlgHom.id R A) f` and of `f` are by definition the
  -- `LinearMap.ker` of `LinearMap.lTensor A f.toLinearMap` and of `f.toLinearMap`.
  exact (Module.Flat.lTensor_exact A f.toLinearMap.exact_subtype_ker_map).linearMap_ker_eq

variable {S D : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Ring D] [Algebra R D]
variable [Algebra S A] [Algebra S B] [IsScalarTower R S A] [IsScalarTower R S B]

/-- The kernel of a tensor product of algebra maps is generated by their kernels when the
first codomain and the quotient of the second domain by its kernel are flat. -/
theorem map_ker_of_flat_flat (f : A →ₐ[S] B) (g : C →ₐ[R] D)
    [Module.Flat R B] [Module.Flat R (C ⧸ RingHom.ker g)] :
    RingHom.ker (map f g) =
      (RingHom.ker f).map (includeLeft : A →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] C) ⊔
        (RingHom.ker g).map (includeRight : C →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] C) := by
  let qf := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ S (RingHom.ker f)
  let qg := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (RingHom.ker g)
  have hf : (Ideal.kerLiftAlg f).comp qf = f := AlgHom.ext (Ideal.kerLiftAlg_mk f)
  have hg : (Ideal.kerLiftAlg g).comp qg = g := AlgHom.ext (Ideal.kerLiftAlg_mk g)
  have hinj : Function.Injective (map (Ideal.kerLiftAlg f) (Ideal.kerLiftAlg g)).toRingHom :=
    map_injective_of_flat_flat _ _ (Ideal.kerLiftAlg_injective f) (Ideal.kerLiftAlg_injective g)
  have hmap : map f g = (map (Ideal.kerLiftAlg f) (Ideal.kerLiftAlg g)).comp (map qf qg) := by
    rw [← map_comp, hf, hg]
  have hker : RingHom.ker (map f g) = RingHom.ker (map qf qg) := by
    rw [hmap, AlgHom.ker_coe, AlgHom.comp_toRingHom]
    exact RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _ hinj
  have hkf : RingHom.ker qf = RingHom.ker f := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_ker (R₁ := S) _
  have hkg : RingHom.ker qg = RingHom.ker g := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_ker (R₁ := R) _
  rw [hker]
  simpa only [hkf, hkg] using
    map_ker qf qg (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_surjective S _) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_surjective R _)

end Ring

end Algebra.TensorProduct

namespace Module

open TensorProduct

variable {R B M : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommSemiring B] [Algebra R B]
  [AddCommMonoid M] [Module R M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower R B M]

/-- If `A` is a flat `B`-module and `M` is a `B`-module which is flat over `R`, then `A ⊗[B] M`
is flat over `R`. This holds for commutative semirings, with `Module.Flat` meaning mono-flatness.
Compare Mathlib's instance for `Module.Flat S (M ⊗[R] N)`, where the semiring `S`
acting on the left factor is an algebra over the base `R` of the tensor product rather than below
it. -/
theorem Flat.tensorProduct_of_flat (A : Type*) [AddCommMonoid A] [Module R A] [Module B A]
    [IsScalarTower R B A] [Flat B A] [Flat R M] : Flat R (A ⊗[B] M) := by
  rw [Flat.iff_lTensor_injectiveₛ]
  intro P _ _ N
  -- Through `(A ⊗[B] M) ⊗[R] N ≃ A ⊗[B] (M ⊗[R] N)`, the map is `A ⊗[B] (M ⊗[R] N ↪ M ⊗[R] P)`.
  have h : N.subtype.lTensor (A ⊗[B] M) =
      ((AlgebraTensorModule.assoc R B B A M P).symm.restrictScalars R).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        ((AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor B M N.subtype).lTensor A).restrictScalars R ∘ₗ
        ((AlgebraTensorModule.assoc R B B A M N).restrictScalars R).toLinearMap := by
    refine TensorProduct.ext' fun x n ↦ ?_
    induction x with
    | tmul a m => simp
    | add x y hx hy => simp only [add_tmul, map_add, hx, hy]
  rw [h]
  simp only [LinearMap.coe_comp, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars,
    EquivLike.comp_injective, EquivLike.injective_comp]
  apply Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap
  rw [AlgebraTensorModule.coe_lTensor]
  exact Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap _ N.injective_subtype

/-- If `C` is a flat `B`-algebra and `J` is an ideal of `B` with `B ⧸ J` flat over `R`, then
`C ⧸ J C ≃ C ⊗[B] (B ⧸ J)` is flat over `R`. A localization `B_q ⧸ J B_q` is the typical
case. -/
theorem Flat.quotient_map_algebraMap {R B : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing B] [Algebra R B]
    (C : Type*) [CommRing C] [Algebra B C] [Algebra R C] [IsScalarTower R B C] [Flat B C]
    (J : Ideal B) [Flat R (B ⧸ J)] : Flat R (C ⧸ J.map (algebraMap B C)) := by
  have := Flat.tensorProduct_of_flat (R := R) (B := B) (M := B ⧸ J) C
  exact Flat.of_linearEquiv
    ((Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot C J).toLinearEquiv.restrictScalars R)

end Module

namespace Module

open TensorProduct LinearMap

variable {R M : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [AddCommMonoid M] [Module R M]

/-- If `f.rTensor M` is injective and `F` is flat, then `(f.rTensor F).rTensor M` is injective.
This holds for commutative semirings, with `Module.Flat` meaning mono-flatness. -/
theorem Flat.rTensor_rTensor_injective {N P : Type*} [AddCommMonoid N] [Module R N]
    [AddCommMonoid P] [Module R P] (F : Type*) [AddCommMonoid F] [Module R F] [Flat R F]
    {f : N →ₗ[R] P} (hf : Function.Injective (f.rTensor M)) :
    Function.Injective ((f.rTensor F).rTensor M) := by
  have h : (rightComm R P F M).toLinearMap ∘ₗ (f.rTensor F).rTensor M =
      ((f.rTensor M).rTensor F) ∘ₗ (rightComm R N F M).toLinearMap := by
    ext; simp
  refine .of_comp (f := rightComm R P F M) ?_
  rw [← LinearEquiv.coe_coe, ← coe_comp, h]
  exact (Flat.rTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap _ hf).comp (rightComm R N F M).injective

/-- Let `f : N →ₗ[R] P` be injective and `ψ : M →ₗ[R] F` be a map to a flat module. An element of
`M ⊗[R] N` killed by `f.lTensor M` is killed by `ψ.rTensor N`, since `f.lTensor F` is injective
and commutes with `ψ`. -/
theorem Flat.rTensor_apply_eq_zero_of_lTensor_apply_eq_zero {N P F : Type*} [AddCommMonoid N]
    [Module R N] [AddCommMonoid P] [Module R P] [AddCommMonoid F] [Module R F] [Flat R F]
    (ψ : M →ₗ[R] F) {f : N →ₗ[R] P} (hf : Function.Injective f) {x : M ⊗[R] N}
    (hx : f.lTensor M x = 0) : ψ.rTensor N x = 0 :=
  Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap f hf <| by
    rw [map_zero, ← comp_apply, lTensor_comp_rTensor, ← rTensor_comp_lTensor, comp_apply, hx,
      map_zero]

end Module

namespace Ideal

open TensorProduct LinearMap

variable {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- If `M ⧸ I M` is flat over `R ⧸ I`, tensoring with `M` preserves injectivity of maps into a
module killed by `I`. -/
theorem rTensor_injective_of_isTorsionBySet (I : Ideal R)
    [Module.Flat (R ⧸ I) (M ⧸ I • (⊤ : Submodule R M))] {K L : Type*} [AddCommGroup K]
    [Module R K] [AddCommGroup L] [Module R L] (hL : Module.IsTorsionBySet R L I)
    {f : K →ₗ[R] L} (hf : Function.Injective f) : Function.Injective (f.rTensor M) := by
  have hK : Module.IsTorsionBySet R K I := fun x a ↦ hf (by rw [map_smul, hL, map_zero])
  let _ := hK.module
  let _ := hL.module
  let A := R ⧸ I
  have hA : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R A) := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  let g : K →ₗ[A] L := f.extendScalarsOfSurjective hA
  have : Module.Flat A (A ⊗[R] M) := .of_linearEquiv
    ((quotTensorEquivQuotSMul M I).extendScalarsOfSurjective hA)
  let eK := AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R A A K M
  let eL := AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R A A L M
  have key (y : K ⊗[A] (A ⊗[R] M)) : f.rTensor M (eK y) = eL (g.rTensor _ y) := by
    induction y using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | add y z hy hz => simp only [map_add, hy, hz]
    | tmul k t =>
      induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
      | add s t hs ht => simp only [tmul_add, map_add, hs, ht]
      | tmul a m =>
        simp only [eK, eL, AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange_tmul, rTensor_tmul]
        rw [← map_smul g]
        exact congrArg (· ⊗ₜ[R] m) (extendScalarsOfSurjective_apply hA f (a • k)).symm
  intro x y hxy
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := eK.surjective x
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := eK.surjective y
  rw [key, key, eL.injective.eq_iff] at hxy
  rw [Module.Flat.rTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap g hf hxy]

section

variable (I : Ideal R) [Module.Flat (R ⧸ I) (M ⧸ I • (⊤ : Submodule R M))]

/-- For a flat module `F`, a submodule `G ⊇ I F` has `G ⊗[R] M → F ⊗[R] M` injective. -/
private theorem subtype_rTensor_injective_of_flat
    (hI : Function.Injective (I.subtype.rTensor M))
    {F : Type*} [AddCommGroup F] [Module R F] [Module.Flat R F] {G : Submodule R F}
    (hIG : I • ⊤ ≤ G) : Function.Injective (G.subtype.rTensor M) := by
  -- The image of `I ⊗ F` in `F` is `I F ⊆ G`, and `G ⧸ I F` is a submodule of `F ⧸ I F`, a module
  -- killed by `I`.
  let φ : I ⊗[R] F →ₗ[R] F := (TensorProduct.lid R F).toLinearMap ∘ₗ I.subtype.rTensor F
  have hφ : range φ = I • ⊤ := I.subtype_rTensor_range F
  let μ : I ⊗[R] F →ₗ[R] G := φ.codRestrict G fun x ↦ hIG (hφ ▸ mem_range_self φ x)
  let K : Submodule R (F ⧸ (I • ⊤ : Submodule R F)) := G.map (I • ⊤ : Submodule R F).mkQ
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hμq, hqK⟩ := G.exists_exact_codRestrict_mkQ (I • ⊤) (f := μ) fun g ↦ by
    rw [← hφ]
    exact ⟨fun ⟨u, hu⟩ ↦ ⟨u, congr_arg Subtype.val hu⟩, fun ⟨u, hu⟩ ↦ ⟨u, Subtype.ext hu⟩⟩
  have hKinj := I.rTensor_injective_of_isTorsionBySet (M := M)
    (Module.isTorsionBySet_quotient_ideal_smul F I) K.injective_subtype
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).mpr fun t ht ↦ ?_
  have hqt : q.rTensor M t = 0 := hKinj <| by
    rw [← rTensor_comp_apply, map_zero, hqK, rTensor_comp_apply, ht, map_zero]
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := (rTensor_exact M hμq hq t).mp hqt
  have hu : φ.rTensor M u = 0 := by
    rw [← ht, ← rTensor_comp_apply, subtype_comp_codRestrict]
  have hφinj : Function.Injective (φ.rTensor M) := by
    rw [rTensor_comp, coe_comp]
    exact (LinearEquiv.rTensor M (TensorProduct.lid R F)).injective.comp
      (Module.Flat.rTensor_rTensor_injective F hI)
  rw [hφinj (hu.trans (map_zero _).symm), map_zero]

/-- If `L ⧸ N` is killed by `I`, then `N ⊗[R] M → L ⊗[R] M` is injective; the proof chases along
a flat module `F` mapping onto `L`. -/
private theorem subtype_rTensor_injective_of_surjective
    (hI : Function.Injective (I.subtype.rTensor M))
    {F L : Type*} [AddCommGroup F] [Module R F] [Module.Flat R F] [AddCommGroup L] [Module R L]
    {π : F →ₗ[R] L} (hπ : Function.Surjective π) {N : Submodule R L} (hN : I • ⊤ ≤ N) :
    Function.Injective (N.subtype.rTensor M) := by
  have hIG : I • ⊤ ≤ N.comap π := Submodule.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp <| by
    rw [Submodule.map_smul'']
    exact (Submodule.smul_mono le_rfl le_top).trans hN
  have hG := subtype_rTensor_injective_of_flat I hI hIG
  -- A diagram chase along `π`.
  let π' : N.comap π →ₗ[R] N := π.restrict fun _ hx ↦ hx
  have hπ' : Function.Surjective π' := fun n ↦
    let ⟨x, hx⟩ := hπ n
    ⟨⟨x, Submodule.mem_comap.mpr (hx ▸ n.property)⟩, Subtype.ext hx⟩
  have hsq : π ∘ₗ (N.comap π).subtype = N.subtype ∘ₗ π' := (subtype_comp_restrict _).symm
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).mpr fun t ht ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := rTensor_surjective M hπ' t
  have hs : π.rTensor M ((N.comap π).subtype.rTensor M s) = 0 := by
    rw [← rTensor_comp_apply, hsq, rTensor_comp_apply, ht]
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := (rTensor_exact M (exact_subtype_ker_map π) hπ _).mp hs
  have hker : ker π ≤ N.comap π := fun x hx ↦
    Submodule.mem_comap.mpr (mem_ker.mp hx ▸ N.zero_mem)
  have hsu : s = (Submodule.inclusion hker).rTensor M u := hG <| by
    rw [← hu, ← rTensor_comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_comp_inclusion]
  rw [hsu, ← rTensor_comp_apply]
  have : π' ∘ₗ Submodule.inclusion hker = 0 := by
    ext x
    exact mem_ker.mp x.property
  rw [this, rTensor_zero, LinearMap.zero_apply]

/-- Let `M ⧸ I M` be flat over `R ⧸ I` and `I ⊗[R] M → M` injective. If `L ⧸ N` is killed by `I`,
then `N ⊗[R] M → L ⊗[R] M` is injective. -/
theorem subtype_rTensor_injective_of_smul_top_le
    (hI : Function.Injective (I.subtype.rTensor M))
    {L : Type*} [AddCommGroup L] [Module R L] {N : Submodule R L} (hN : I • ⊤ ≤ N) :
    Function.Injective (N.subtype.rTensor M) :=
  subtype_rTensor_injective_of_surjective I hI (π := Finsupp.linearCombination R id)
    (fun l ↦ ⟨Finsupp.single l 1, by simp⟩) hN

/-- Let `M ⧸ I M` be flat over `R ⧸ I` and `I ⊗[R] M → M` injective. If `L ⧸ N` is killed by
`I ^ n`, then `N ⊗[R] M → L ⊗[R] M` is injective. -/
theorem subtype_rTensor_injective_of_pow_smul_top_le
    (hI : Function.Injective (I.subtype.rTensor M))
    (n : ℕ) {L : Type*} [AddCommGroup L] [Module R L] {N : Submodule R L} (hN : I ^ n • ⊤ ≤ N) :
    Function.Injective (N.subtype.rTensor M) := by
  induction n generalizing N with
  | zero =>
    refine I.subtype_rTensor_injective_of_smul_top_le hI (le_trans ?_ hN)
    rw [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
    exact Submodule.smul_mono_left le_top
  | succ n ih =>
    -- `N ⊆ N' = N + Iⁿ L ⊆ L`, where `I` kills `N' ⧸ N` and `Iⁿ` kills `L ⧸ N'`.
    set N' := N ⊔ I ^ n • ⊤
    have hle : N ≤ N' := le_sup_left
    have hN₀ : I • ⊤ ≤ N.comap N'.subtype := Submodule.smul_le.mpr fun i hi x _ ↦ by
      obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, hyz⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp x.property
      have hiz : i • z ∈ I ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule R L) := by
        rw [pow_succ', Submodule.mul_smul]
        exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul hi hz
      simpa [← hyz] using N.add_mem (N.smul_mem i hy) (hN hiz)
    have h₀ := I.subtype_rTensor_injective_of_smul_top_le hI hN₀
    have hsub : N.subtype = N'.subtype ∘ₗ (N.comap N'.subtype).subtype ∘ₗ
        (Submodule.comapSubtypeEquivOfLe hle).symm.toLinearMap := by
      ext; simp
    rw [hsub, rTensor_comp, rTensor_comp, coe_comp, coe_comp]
    exact (ih le_sup_right).comp (h₀.comp (LinearEquiv.rTensor M _).injective)

/-- For ideals `J` and `P`, if `(J ⧸ (J ⊓ P)) ⊗[R] M → (R ⧸ P) ⊗[R] M` is injective, then every
element of the kernel of `J ⊗[R] M → M` comes from `(J ⊓ P) ⊗[R] M`. -/
private theorem mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_of_injective {J P : Ideal R}
    (hN : Function.Injective ((Submodule.map P.mkQ J).subtype.rTensor M)) {t : J ⊗[R] M}
    (ht : J.subtype.rTensor M t = 0) :
    t ∈ range ((Submodule.inclusion (inf_le_left : J ⊓ P ≤ J)).rTensor M) := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hexact, hqN⟩ := Submodule.exists_exact_codRestrict_mkQ J P
    (f := Submodule.inclusion (inf_le_left : J ⊓ P ≤ J)) fun j ↦ by
      simp [Submodule.range_inclusion]
  refine (rTensor_exact M hexact hq t).mp (hN ?_)
  rw [← rTensor_comp_apply, map_zero, hqN, rTensor_comp_apply, ht, map_zero]

/-- Let `M ⧸ I M` be flat over `R ⧸ I` and `I ⊗[R] M → M` injective. For an ideal `J`, every
element of the kernel of `J ⊗[R] M → M` comes from `(J ⊓ I ^ n) ⊗[R] M`. -/
theorem mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_pow (hI : Function.Injective (I.subtype.rTensor M))
    (n : ℕ) {J : Ideal R} {t : J ⊗[R] M} (ht : J.subtype.rTensor M t = 0) :
    t ∈ range ((Submodule.inclusion (inf_le_left : J ⊓ I ^ n ≤ J)).rTensor M) := by
  -- `J ⧸ (J ⊓ Iⁿ)` is a submodule of `R ⧸ Iⁿ`, a module killed by `Iⁿ`.
  have hL : Module.IsTorsionBySet R (R ⧸ I ^ n) ↑(I ^ n) :=
    (Module.isTorsionBySet_quotient_iff (I ^ n) _).mpr fun x _ hr ↦ (I ^ n).mul_mem_right x hr
  exact mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_of_injective
    (I.subtype_rTensor_injective_of_pow_smul_top_le hI n <| Submodule.smul_le.mpr
      fun r hr x _ ↦ (hL (a := ⟨r, hr⟩) : r • x = 0) ▸ Submodule.zero_mem _) ht

end

/-- Let `M ⧸ P M` be flat over `R ⧸ P`. For an ideal `J`, every element of the kernel of
`J ⊗[R] M → M` comes from `(J ⊓ P) ⊗[R] M`. -/
theorem mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_of_flat (P : Ideal R)
    [Module.Flat (R ⧸ P) (M ⧸ P • (⊤ : Submodule R M))] {J : Ideal R} {t : J ⊗[R] M}
    (ht : J.subtype.rTensor M t = 0) :
    t ∈ range ((Submodule.inclusion (inf_le_left : J ⊓ P ≤ J)).rTensor M) := by
  -- `J ⧸ (J ⊓ P)` is a submodule of `R ⧸ P`, and both are killed by `P`.
  have hL : Module.IsTorsionBySet R (R ⧸ P) P :=
    (Module.isTorsionBySet_quotient_iff P _).mpr fun x _ hr ↦ P.mul_mem_right x hr
  exact mem_range_rTensor_inclusion_inf_of_injective
    (P.rTensor_injective_of_isTorsionBySet hL (Submodule.injective_subtype _)) ht

end Ideal

namespace RingHom

open scoped nonZeroDivisors

/-- If `A` and `B` are flat domains over `R` and a ring map `ψ` out of `A ⊗[R] B` has kernel `P`
disjoint from the nonzerodivisors, then `ψ` is injective on both tensor factors. -/
theorem injective_comp_include_of_disjoint_nonZeroDivisors {R A B L : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [Algebra R A] [Algebra R B]
    [Module.Flat R A] [Module.Flat R B] [Ring L] (ψ : A ⊗[R] B →+* L) (P : Ideal (A ⊗[R] B))
    (hψ : ∀ x, ψ x = 0 ↔ x ∈ P)
    (hdisj : Disjoint (P : Set (A ⊗[R] B)) (nonZeroDivisors (A ⊗[R] B))) :
    Function.Injective (ψ.comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom) ∧
      Function.Injective
        (ψ.comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : B →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] B).toRingHom) := by
  refine ⟨(injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).mpr fun b hb ↦ by_contra fun hb0 ↦ ?_,
    (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).mpr fun c hc ↦ by_contra fun hc0 ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact Set.disjoint_left.mp hdisj ((hψ _).mp hb)
      (Module.Flat.algebraMap_mem_nonZeroDivisors (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hb0))
  · have hc' := Module.Flat.algebraMap_mem_nonZeroDivisors (A := B ⊗[R] A)
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hc0)
    exact Set.disjoint_left.mp hdisj ((hψ _).mp hc)
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_injective (f := Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R A B)
        (AlgEquiv.injective _) (by simpa using hc'))

end RingHom

namespace Module

section TensorKernel

open TensorProduct

variable {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- If a module over an algebra is flat over the base at every prime not containing `a`,
powers of `a` kill every element of a tensor kernel induced by an injective base-linear map.
No finiteness hypothesis is needed. -/
theorem pow_smul_eq_zero_of_flat_localizedModule {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    [Module S M] [IsScalarTower R S M] {a : S}
    (ha : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum S, a ∉ p.asIdeal →
      Module.Flat R (LocalizedModule p.asIdeal.primeCompl M))
    {N N' : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [AddCommGroup N'] [Module R N']
    (f : N →ₗ[R] N') (hf : Function.Injective f) (t : M ⊗[R] N)
    (ht : f.lTensor M t = 0) : ∃ n : ℕ, a ^ n • t = 0 := by
  let I : Ideal S := LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton S _ t)
  have haI : a ∈ I.radical := by
    rw [Ideal.radical_eq_sInf, Submodule.mem_sInf]
    rintro (p : Ideal S) ⟨hIp, hp⟩
    by_contra hap
    let _ := hp
    have : Module.Flat R (LocalizedModule p.primeCompl M) := ha ⟨p, hp⟩ hap
    let l := LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap p.primeCompl M
    have hg : AlgebraTensorModule.rTensor R N l t = 0 := by
      -- The algebra-linear localization map has this restricted base-linear tensor map.
      change (l.restrictScalars R).rTensor N t = 0
      exact Module.Flat.rTensor_apply_eq_zero_of_lTensor_apply_eq_zero (l.restrictScalars R) hf ht
    obtain ⟨scalar, hs⟩ := (IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff p.primeCompl
      (f := AlgebraTensorModule.rTensor R N l)).mp hg
    exact scalar.property (hIp hs)
  exact haI

/-- If `M` is flat over `R ⧸ p` away from `a`, powers of `a` kill tensor kernels of injective
`R`-linear maps into modules annihilated by `p`. -/
theorem pow_smul_eq_zero_of_flat_localizedModule_quotient (p : Ideal R) [Module (R ⧸ p) M]
    [IsScalarTower R (R ⧸ p) M] (a : R)
    (hflat : ∀ q : PrimeSpectrum (R ⧸ p), Ideal.Quotient.mk p a ∉ q.asIdeal →
      Module.Flat (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) (LocalizedModule q.asIdeal.primeCompl M)) :
    ∀ (N N' : Type*) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [AddCommGroup N'] [Module R N'],
      (∀ r ∈ p, ∀ n : N', r • n = 0) →
      ∀ f : N →ₗ[R] N', Function.Injective f → ∀ t : M ⊗[R] N,
        f.lTensor M t = 0 → ∃ n : ℕ, a ^ n • t = 0 := by
  intro N N' _ _ _ _ hN' f hf t ht
  have hN : ∀ r ∈ p, ∀ n : N, r • n = 0 := fun r hr n ↦
    hf (by rw [map_smul, hN' r hr (f n), map_zero])
  have hNt : Module.IsTorsionBySet R N p := fun n r ↦ hN r r.property n
  have hN't : Module.IsTorsionBySet R N' p := fun n r ↦ hN' r r.property n
  let _ := hNt.module
  let _ := hN't.module
  let f' : N →ₗ[R ⧸ p] N' :=
    { toFun := f
      map_add' := f.map_add
      map_smul' := by
        rintro ⟨r⟩ n
        exact f.map_smul r n }
  -- The quotient-linear lift keeps the original underlying map.
  have hf' : f'.restrictScalars R = f := rfl
  let e := quotientScalarEquiv p M N
  let e' := quotientScalarEquiv p M N'
  have hflat' (q : PrimeSpectrum (R ⧸ p)) (haq : Ideal.Quotient.mk p a ∉ q.asIdeal) :
      Module.Flat (R ⧸ p) (LocalizedModule q.asIdeal.primeCompl M) := by
    have := hflat q haq
    exact Module.Flat.trans (R ⧸ p) (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) _
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := pow_smul_eq_zero_of_flat_localizedModule
    (a := Ideal.Quotient.mk p a) hflat' f' hf (e.symm t) (by
      apply e'.injective
      rw [quotientScalarEquiv_lTensor, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply, hf', ht, map_zero])
  refine ⟨n, ?_⟩
  have hn' := congrArg e hn
  rw [← map_pow, ← Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq, algebraMap_smul, map_smul,
    LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply, map_zero] at hn'
  exact hn'

end TensorKernel

end Module

/-! ### Tensor kernels for finite-model approximation -/

open TensorProduct LinearMap
open scoped Pointwise

namespace Module.Flat

variable {R : Type*} {M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
  [Module R M]

/-- If scalars outside an ideal act bijectively on a module, tensoring by that module preserves
inclusions between modules annihilated by the ideal. -/
theorem _root_.Ideal.lTensor_subtype_injective_of_bijective_smul
    (I : Ideal R)
    (hM : ∀ coefficient ∉ I, Function.Bijective (fun m : M ↦
      coefficient • m)) {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module R N] (hN : ∀ r ∈ I, ∀ x : N, r
      • x = 0) (N' : Submodule R N) :
    Function.Injective (N'.subtype.lTensor M) := by
  have : Flat (R ⧸ I) (M ⧸ I • (⊤ : Submodule R M))
    := by
    refine of_bijective_smul fun coefficient hr ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨coefficient, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective coefficient
    have hrp : coefficient ∉ I := fun h ↦ hr (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr
      h)
    let e := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (DistribSMul.toLinearMap R M
      coefficient) (hM coefficient hrp)
    have hsmul (m : M) : (Ideal.Quotient.mk I coefficient) •
        (Submodule.Quotient.mk m : M ⧸ I • (⊤ : Submodule R
          M)) =
          Submodule.Quotient.mk (coefficient • m) := rfl
    constructor
    · intro x y hxy
      induction x using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with | H x =>
      induction y using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with | H y =>
      simp only [hsmul, Submodule.Quotient.eq] at hxy ⊢
      have := Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top I e.symm.toLinearMap hxy
      rw [Submodule.mem_comap, ← smul_sub] at this
      convert this using 1
      exact (e.symm_apply_apply (x - y)).symm
    · intro x
      induction x using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with | H x =>
      refine ⟨Submodule.Quotient.mk (e.symm x), ?_⟩
      -- The quotient action is induced from the scalar action on representatives.
      change _ • _ = _
      rw [hsmul]
      congr 1
      exact e.apply_symm_apply x
  exact (N'.subtype.lTensor_inj_iff_rTensor_inj M).mpr
    (I.rTensor_injective_of_isTorsionBySet
      (fun x r ↦ hN r r.property x) N'.injective_subtype)

end Module.Flat
namespace Module.Flat

universe u
variable {R : Type u} {M : Type*} [CommRing R]
  [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (I : Ideal R)

private lemma exists_lTensor_smul_top_preimage
    (hQ : ∀ (N : Type u) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N],
      (∀ a ∈ I, ∀ n : N, a • n = 0) →
      ∀ N' : Submodule R N, Function.Injective (N'.subtype.lTensor M))
    {F : Type u} [AddCommGroup F] [Module R F]
    (K : Submodule R F)
    (hK : I • (⊤ : Submodule R F) ≤ K)
    (z : M ⊗[R] K)
    (hz : K.subtype.lTensor M z = 0) :
    ∃ w : M ⊗[R] ↥(I • (⊤ : Submodule R F)),
      (Submodule.inclusion hK).lTensor M w = z ∧
        (I • (⊤ : Submodule R F)).subtype.lTensor M w =
          0 := by
  set IF := I • (⊤ : Submodule R F)
  let K' : Submodule R (F ⧸ IF) := K.map IF.mkQ
  let q : K →ₗ[R] K' := (IF.mkQ.restrict fun x hx ↦
    Submodule.mem_map_of_mem hx)
  have hq : Function.Surjective q := by
    rintro ⟨_, x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, rfl⟩
  have hex : Function.Exact (Submodule.inclusion hK) q := by
    intro x
    constructor
    · intro h
      have : (x : F) ∈ IF := by
        simpa [q, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] using
          congr(($h : F ⧸ IF))
      exact ⟨⟨x, this⟩, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
      apply Subtype.ext
      simp [q, (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero IF).mpr y.property]
  have hkill : ∀ r ∈ I, ∀ x : F ⧸ IF, r • x = 0 := by
    intro r hi x
    induction x using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
    | H x =>
      rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul hi trivial
  have hQ' := hQ _ hkill K'
  have hcomm : K'.subtype ∘ₗ q = IF.mkQ ∘ₗ K.subtype := by ext; rfl
  have h1 : q.lTensor M z = 0 := by
    apply hQ'
    rw [map_zero, ← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.lTensor_comp, hcomm,
      LinearMap.lTensor_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply, hz, map_zero]
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := ((_root_.lTensor_exact M hex hq) z).1 h1
  refine ⟨w, rfl, ?_⟩
  rw [← hz, ← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.lTensor_comp]
  rfl

private lemma map_eq_zero_of_lTensor_subtype_eq_zero_of_flat
    (hQ : ∀ (N : Type u) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R
      N], (∀ r ∈ I, ∀ x : N, r • x = 0) →
      ∀ N' : Submodule R N, Function.Injective (N'.subtype.lTensor M))
    {F : Type u} [AddCommGroup F] [Module R F] [Flat R
      F] (K : Submodule R F)
    (hK : I • (⊤ : Submodule R F) ≤ K) {P : Type*}
      [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P]
    (ψ : M ⊗[R] K →ₗ[R] P)
    (hψ : ∀ ξ : M ⊗[R] I, TensorProduct.rid R M
      (I.subtype.lTensor M ξ) = 0 → ∀ x : F,
      ψ ((((toSpanSingleton R F x) ∘ₗ I.subtype).codRestrict K
        fun r ↦ hK (Submodule.smul_mem_smul r.property trivial)).lTensor
          M ξ) = 0)
    (z : M ⊗[R] K) (hz : K.subtype.lTensor M
      z = 0) : ψ z = 0 := by
  set IF := I • (⊤ : Submodule R F)
  obtain ⟨w, rfl, h2⟩ :=
    exists_lTensor_smul_top_preimage I hQ K hK z hz
  let ν : I ⊗[R] F →ₗ[R] IF := (TensorProduct.lid R
    F ∘ₗ I.subtype.rTensor F).codRestrict IF
    fun x ↦ by
      induction x with
      | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy
      | tmul r x => exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul r.property trivial
  have hν : Function.Surjective ν := by
    rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
    induction hy using Submodule.smul_induction_on' with
    | smul r hi x _ => exact ⟨⟨r, hi⟩ ⊗ₜ x, rfl⟩
    | add x hx y hy hx' hy' =>
      obtain ⟨factor, ha⟩ := hx'
      obtain ⟨otherFactor, hb⟩ := hy'
      exact ⟨factor + otherFactor, by rw [map_add, ha, hb]; rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := LinearMap.lTensor_surjective M hν w
  set μ : M ⊗[R] I →ₗ[R] M := (TensorProduct.rid R
    M).toLinearMap ∘ₗ I.subtype.lTensor M
  have hΦ : (IF.subtype ∘ₗ ν).lTensor M ∘ₗ (TensorProduct.assoc R
    M I F).toLinearMap =
      μ.rTensor F := by
    ext m r x
    simp [ν, μ, smul_tmul]
  have hΨ : μ.rTensor F ((TensorProduct.assoc R M I F).symm
    v) = 0 := by
    rw [← hΦ, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply,
      LinearMap.lTensor_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply, h2]
  have hexμ : Function.Exact (LinearMap.ker μ).subtype μ := LinearMap.exact_subtype_ker_map μ
  obtain ⟨witness, hw⟩ := ((rTensor_exact F hexμ) _).1 hΨ
  rw [← LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply (TensorProduct.assoc R M I F)
    v, ← hw]
  have key (parameter : M ⊗[R] I) (x : F) :
      (Submodule.inclusion hK).lTensor M (ν.lTensor M (TensorProduct.assoc
        R M I F (parameter ⊗ₜ x))) =
        (((toSpanSingleton R F x) ∘ₗ I.subtype).codRestrict K
          fun r ↦ hK (Submodule.smul_mem_smul r.property trivial)).lTensor
            M parameter :=
            by
    induction parameter with
    | add x y hx hy => rw [add_tmul, map_add, map_add, map_add, hx, hy, map_add]
    | tmul m r => rfl
  clear hw
  induction witness with
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy, add_zero]
  | tmul ξ x =>
    rw [LinearMap.rTensor_tmul, Submodule.subtype_apply, key]
    exact hψ ξ ξ.property x

/-- A tensor criterion for injectivity of a submodule inclusion containing the ideal multiple of
the ambient module: injectivity modulo the ideal and vanishing on its tensor kernel suffice. -/
theorem _root_.Ideal.lTensor_subtype_injective_of_forall_ker
    (hQ : ∀ (N : Type u) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R
      N], (∀ r ∈ I, ∀ x : N, r • x = 0) →
      ∀ N' : Submodule R N, Function.Injective (N'.subtype.lTensor M))
    {N : Type u} [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N]
      (L : Submodule R N)
    (hL : I • (⊤ : Submodule R N) ≤ L)
    (hK : ∀ ξ : M ⊗[R] I, TensorProduct.rid R M
      (I.subtype.lTensor M ξ) = 0 → ∀ x : N,
      (((toSpanSingleton R N x) ∘ₗ I.subtype).codRestrict
        L
        fun r ↦ hL (Submodule.smul_mem_smul r.property trivial)).lTensor
          M ξ = 0) :
    Function.Injective (L.subtype.lTensor M) := by
  let F := N →₀ R
  let φ : F →ₗ[R] N := Finsupp.linearCombination R _root_.id
  have hφ : Function.Surjective φ := fun x ↦
    ⟨Finsupp.single x 1, by rw [Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul]; rfl⟩
  let LF : Submodule R F := L.comap φ
  have hLF : I • (⊤ : Submodule R F) ≤ LF := by
    rw [Submodule.smul_le]
    intro r hi x _
    -- Membership in the inverse-image submodule is membership after applying the map.
    change φ (r • x) ∈ L
    rw [map_smul]
    exact hL (Submodule.smul_mem_smul hi trivial)
  let φL : LF →ₗ[R] L := φ.restrict fun x hx ↦ hx
  have hφL : Function.Surjective φL := by
    rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hφ y
    exact ⟨⟨x, hy⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := LinearMap.lTensor_surjective M hφL x
  have hsq : L.subtype ∘ₗ φL = φ ∘ₗ LF.subtype := by ext; rfl
  have hz : φ.lTensor M (LF.subtype.lTensor M y) = 0 := by
    rw [← LinearMap.comp_apply (φ.lTensor M), ← LinearMap.lTensor_comp, ← hsq,
      LinearMap.lTensor_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply, hx]
  obtain ⟨witness, hw⟩ := ((_root_.lTensor_exact (R := R)
    (M := ↥(LinearMap.ker φ)) (N := F) (P := N)
    (f := (LinearMap.ker φ).subtype) (g := φ) M
    (LinearMap.exact_subtype_ker_map φ) hφ) _).1 hz
  have hle : LinearMap.ker φ ≤ LF := fun x hx ↦ by
    -- The inverse-image submodule is defined by membership of the image.
    change φ x ∈ L
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hx]
    exact zero_mem _
  have hzero : φL ∘ₗ Submodule.inclusion hle = 0 := by
    ext x; exact congr(($(LinearMap.mem_ker.mp x.property) : N))
  have hw' : φL.lTensor M ((Submodule.inclusion hle).lTensor M witness) = 0 := by
    rw [← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.lTensor_comp, hzero]
    simp
  have hdiff : LF.subtype.lTensor M (y - (Submodule.inclusion hle).lTensor
    M witness) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, sub_eq_zero, ← hw, ← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.lTensor_comp]
    rfl
  have := map_eq_zero_of_lTensor_subtype_eq_zero_of_flat I hQ LF hLF (φL.lTensor M)
    (fun ξ hk x ↦ by
      rw [← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.lTensor_comp]
      convert hK ξ hk (φ x) using 3
      ext r
      simp [φL, φ, LinearMap.restrict_apply])
    _ hdiff
  rwa [map_sub, hw', sub_zero] at this

end Module.Flat

namespace Module

variable {R₀ A S₀ : Type*} [CommRing R₀] [CommRing A] [Algebra R₀ A]
  [CommRing S₀] [Algebra R₀ S₀]

/-- Flatness after base change preserves tensor inclusions of ideals over the larger base. -/
theorem rTensor_ideal_subtype_injective_of_flat_baseChange
    [Flat A (A ⊗[R₀] S₀)] (I : Ideal A) :
    Function.Injective (AlgebraTensorModule.rTensor R₀ S₀ I.subtype) := by
  have hflat := Flat.rTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap
    (M := A ⊗[R₀] S₀) I.subtype Subtype.val_injective
  have hcomm : ∀ x, AlgebraTensorModule.rTensor R₀ S₀ I.subtype
      (AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ A A I S₀ x) =
        AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ A A A S₀
          (I.subtype.rTensor _ x) := by
    intro x
    induction x with
    | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy, map_add, map_add]
    | tmul otherIndex y =>
      induction y with
      | add y z hy hz => simp only [tmul_add, map_add, hy, hz]
      | tmul factor scalar => simp
  intro x y hxy
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ :=
    (AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ A A I S₀).surjective x
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ :=
    (AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ A A I S₀).surjective y
  rw [hcomm, hcomm] at hxy
  rw [hflat ((AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ A A A
    S₀).injective hxy)]

/-- Every tensor-kernel element comes from a finitely generated subideal. -/
theorem exists_fg_ideal_tensor_kernel (I : Ideal R₀) (ξ : S₀ ⊗[R₀] I)
    (hξ : TensorProduct.rid R₀ S₀ (I.subtype.lTensor S₀ ξ) = 0) :
    ∃ (J : Ideal R₀) (_ : J.FG) (hJI : J ≤ I) (ξJ : S₀ ⊗[R₀] J),
      (Submodule.inclusion hJI).lTensor S₀ ξJ = ξ ∧
        TensorProduct.rid R₀ S₀ (J.subtype.lTensor S₀ ξJ) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨J, hJ, hJI, ξ', hξ'⟩ :=
    Submodule.exists_fg_le_eq_rTensor_inclusion (TensorProduct.comm R₀ S₀ I ξ)
  let ξJ := TensorProduct.comm R₀ J S₀ ξ'
  have hinc : (Submodule.inclusion hJI).lTensor S₀ ξJ = ξ := by
    apply (TensorProduct.comm R₀ S₀ I).injective
    rw [LinearMap.lTensor_comm]
    simpa only [TensorProduct.comm_comm] using hξ'.symm
  refine ⟨J, hJ, hJI, ξJ, hinc, ?_⟩
  have hs : I.subtype ∘ₗ Submodule.inclusion hJI = J.subtype := rfl
  rw [← hs, LinearMap.lTensor_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply, hinc]
  exact hξ

end Module
